# Component Rules

## Server vs Client
- Write Server Components by default
- Use the `"use client"` directive only when:
  - Using hooks like `useState`, `useEffect`, `useRef`
  - Attaching event handlers (`onClick`, `onChange`, etc.)
  - Accessing browser APIs
  - Creating context providers

## Component Organization
- Page components: `page.tsx` under `src/app/`
- Shared components: under `src/components/`
- shadcn/ui components: `src/components/ui/` — do not edit manually
- Sub-components for large pages: under `src/app/[route]/_components/`

## Forms and Validation
- Forms use Server Actions (`"use server"`)
- Validation with Zod; schemas defined under `src/server/validations/`
- For instant client-side validation: `react-hook-form` + `zodResolver`

## Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS classes; do not write inline styles
- Use `cn()` utility for component variants (`src/lib/utils.ts`)
- To add a shadcn/ui component: `npx shadcn add <component>`

## TypeScript
- Define a separate interface for props; do not use inline types
- Do not use `React.FC`; use direct function definitions
```ts
// Correct
interface ThreadCardProps {
  thread: Thread
  showCategory?: boolean
}
export function ThreadCard({ thread, showCategory = false }: ThreadCardProps) {}

// Wrong
const ThreadCard: React.FC<{ thread: Thread }> = ({ thread }) => {}
```
